# 2.2.scenario.enumeration.from.literature.stone

## .what

enumerate the candidate scenarios from **bhrowser ground truth** — what the literature + social
corpus actually report as causes of this effect. this stream catches the branch first-principles
logic blind-spots. this is a **research stone**: it gathers cited sources.

## .inputs

- `1.2.intake.structure.yield.md` — the exposures + effects (the search targets)
- the two-stream method: `howto.research-effect-socials-and-formals.[lesson].md`

## .do

- gather via the **bhrowser** only — never WebSearch/WebFetch (`rule.require.bhrowser-citations`)
- pull both streams: **formal** (PMC/FDA/guideline ground truth) and **social/anecdote** (owner
  reports, forum threads with clinician replies)
- read the comments, not just the headline (`rule.require.read-social-comments`)
- for each reported cause, name the scenario + cite the source verbatim

## .emit

into `2.2.scenario.enumeration.from.literature.yield.md` — the literature-derived scenario list, each
with its citation.

## .accrue

lift every generic, cited fact (incidence rates, reported cause frequencies, mechanism facts) into
`accrue/inventory.of=<topic>.md`, case-neutral, per `rule.require.accrue-research`. the case list
stays in the yield; the reusable facts go to `accrue/`.

## .done when

the literature-derived scenario list is complete, each scenario cited (bhrowser-verified), and the
generic facts are accrued.
